## 8. Suggested Question for Gemini

Given the above, the open strategic question worth putting to Gemini is less "how do we patch `AIEngine.js`" and more:
> **Given that the position-reconciliation layer was removed five weeks ago and never rebuilt, and that the risk-debate gate has blocked 100% of new trades for the last two weeks, is the right move to harden the current architecture (P0–P2 above), or to treat this as a checkpoint to redesign the exit/reconciliation layer from scratch before adding any more AI-side features?** The AI decision layer is arguably the most *tested and correct* part of the codebase right now (§4.3) — the actual structural risk is entirely in the broker/database boundary (§2).

